loss":"to live"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to live"},{"surface":"கண்டன்றும்","parts":[{"text":"கண்டன்றும்","lemma":"கண்டன்றும்","gloss":"we have seen indeed"}],"gloss":"we have seen indeed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இலமே","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"not"},{"text":"அம்","lemma":"அம்","gloss":"first person plural suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"we have not"},{"surface":"தாழாது","parts":[{"text":"தாழ்","lemma":"தாழ்","gloss":"to delay/bow down"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ஆது","gloss":"negative adverbial participle suffix"}],"gloss":"without delaying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"திருந்து","parts":[{"text":"திருந்து","lemma":"திருந்து","gloss":"to be perfect/correct"}],"gloss":"perfect"},{"surface":"அடி","parts":[{"text":"அடி","lemma":"அடி","gloss":"foot"}],"gloss":"feet"},{"surface":"பொருந்த","parts":[{"text":"பொருந்து","lemma":"பொருந்து","gloss":"to fit/reach"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to reach"},{"surface":"வல்லோர்","parts":[{"text":"வல்","lemma":"வல்","gloss":"capable"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ஓர்","gloss":"plural suffix"}],"gloss":"those who are capable"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வருந்த","parts":[{"text":"வருந்து","lemma":"வருந்து","gloss":"to suffer"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to suffer"},{"surface":"காண்டல்","parts":[{"text":"காண்","lemma":"காண்","gloss":"to see"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"தல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"seeing"},{"surface":"அதனினும்","parts":[{"text":"அதனினும்","lemma":"அதனினும்","gloss":"even more than that"}],"gloss":"even more than that","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இலமே","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"not"},{"text":"அம்","lemma":"அம்","gloss":"first person plural suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"we have not"}]}],"literal":"Peasant women with hair-knots of short hair and cool leaf-garments / weed out small, excellent blue water-lilies along with white water-lilies / in the wet fields where eels wriggle, chopping the slush / the thick-eyed cut pieces of pond-dwelling vaalai fish / as a side-dish for the white rice of new paddy / they gorge until their rib-sides stretch tight / in the paddy fields of long ears of grain, where sheaves of harvested grain are abundant / the dusty-headed children of strong-handed laborers / when they get bored of the large fallen coconuts / climb the narrow-topped tall haystacks and rise with force / to try and touch the fruits of the fertile-branched palmyra palm / such is the daily fresh fertility of the good country's lord / Cenni of the well-made chariot and broad hands shining with spears / if there are those who oppose his chest adorned with bow-garlands / they themselves will know what is good for them; we / those who fought without fail against his firm shoulders resembling wooden bolts / have never seen them survive; without delaying / those who are capable of reaching and fitting his perfect feet / we have never seen them suffer even more than that","translation":"Peasant women, their short hair tied in knots and wearing cool leaf-garments, weed out small, beautiful blue water-lilies along with white water-lilies from the wet fields where eels wriggle. In that slush, they chop the thick-eyed vaalai fish from the ponds into pieces, and eat them as a side-dish with the white rice of new paddy, gorging until their ribs stretch tight. In these fields of long-eared grain where harvested sheaves lie in abundance, the dusty-headed children of strong-handed laborers, when bored of playing with fallen coconuts, climb the narrow-topped tall haystacks and leap up with force to reach the fruits of the tall palmyra palms. Such is the daily, fresh prosperity of the good land ruled by Cenni, who possesses well-made chariots and broad hands shining with spears. If there are any who dare to oppose his chest adorned with garlands of victory, they will learn what is good for them. We have never seen those who fought against his firm, pillar-like shoulders survive; nor have we ever seen those who hasten to bow at his perfect feet suffer in the least.","modern":"குட்டையான கூந்தலை முடியாக முடித்து, குளிர்ந்த தழையாடை அணிந்த உழத்தியர், விலங்குகள் போன்ற மலங்கு மீன்கள் துள்ளும் வயல்களில், சிறிய அழகிய நெய்தல் மலர்களையும் ஆம்பல் மலர்களையும் களைகின்றனர். அவ்வாறு களைகையில் சேற்றில் அகப்படும் பெரிய கண்களைக் கொண்ட வாளை மீன்களைத் துண்டு துண்டாக வெட்டி, புதிய நெல்லின் வெண்மையான சோற்றுடன் தொடுகறியாகச் சேர்த்து, விலா எலும்புகள் புடைக்கும்படி வயிறார உண்கின்றனர். நீண்ட கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட வயல்களில் நெற்போர் குவித்து வைக்கப்பட்டுள்ளது. வன்மையான கைகளைக் கொண்ட உழவர்களின் புழுதி படிந்த தலையையுடைய சிறுவர்கள், கீழே விழுந்து கிடக்கும் தென்னம்பழங்களை விளையாடிச் சலித்த பின், குறுகிய உச்சியை உடைய நெடிய வைக்கோல் போர்களின் மேல் ஏறி, அங்கிருந்து விசையோடு குதித்து, செழுமையான கிளைகளைக் கொண்ட பனைமரத்தின் பழங்களைத் தொட முயல்கின்றனர். இத்தகைய நாள்தோறும் புதுவருவாய் தரும் வளமான நாட்டின் தலைவன், வேல் விளங்கும் அகன்ற கைகளையும் இயங்கும் தேரையும் உடைய சோழன் சென்னி ஆவான். வில்லால் தொடுக்கப்பட்ட மாலையை அணிந்த அவனது மார்பை எதிர்த்துப் போரிடுபவர் எவரேனும் இருந்தால், அவர்கள் தங்களுக்கு எது நல்லது என்பதைத் தாங்களே அறிந்து கொள்ளட்டும். தூண் போன்ற அவனது வலிய தோள்களை எதிர்த்துப் போரிட்டவர்கள் உயிர் பிழைத்து வாழ்ந்ததை நாம் கண்டதில்லை. அதே வேளையில், அவனது செம்மையான திருவடிகளை விரைந்து சரணடைந்தவர்கள் எவரும் துன்புறுவதையும் நாம் கண்டதில்லை.","explanation":"The poet Kōnāṭṭu Eṟiccilūr Māṭalaṉ Maturai Kumaraṉār addresses the Chola king Nalankilli (referred to as Cenni). The poet praises the immense agricultural wealth of the Chola country, describing the rich lifestyle of the peasants and their children, and contrasts this peaceful prosperity with the king's terrifying might in battle. The vivid description of peasant women feasting on fresh fish and new rice, and children leaping from high haystacks to reach palmyra fruits, paints a picture of effortless abundance. This fertile landscape (marutam) serves as a backdrop to highlight the king's absolute power; his enemies are utterly destroyed, while those who surrender to him enjoy peaceful prosperity. Key words include 'கடைசியர்' (peasant women), 'புதுநெல்' (new paddy), 'யாணர்' (fresh fertility), 'சென்னி' (Chola king), and 'மலைந்தோர்' (those who fought).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}